      "headline": "Story of fake death unfolds",
      "content": "A mainland woman has admitted being in a scam to defraud an insurer by faking a death. Liu Fang, 34, who is six months pregnant, appeared before District Court Judge Ernest Lin Kam-hung yesterday. He heard Dah Sing Insurance received two insurance purchases in the name of mainlander Hou Zhenlian from agent Tong Wai-fung in 2015. And Liu would collect over HK$5 million if Hou died. In May 2016, Liu met with Hou and Tong in Shanxi and they agreed to fake Hou's death. That involved a death certificate from Hou's employer, Yuci Electric Power Supply. Soon after, Liu received a certificate stating Hou died of cardiac arrest on May 26, 2016. Liu then traveled to Hong Kong with Tong to claim from Dah Sing. But the insurer ruled the claim invalid because of a flaw in Hou's medical record. Then the Independent Commission Against Corruption found Hou's employer did not issue a death certificate. And colleagues of Hou said they had seen him a year after he supposedly died. In mitigation, a lawyer said Liu managed a business for Hou. But when it ran into difficulties Tong persuaded the pair to fake Hou's death. The judge said Liu faced a prison term and remanded her in custody to September 17.",
